docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:94:## 3. What Claude Code Forms Early
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:96:Claude Code main forms a line early by **turning behaviors into surfaces and hooks**.
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:114:So the early line formation structure in Claude Code is:
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:121:Claude Code forces line formation through surface and intervention points.
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:178:Claude Code says:
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:225:- Claude Code exposes that our space still lacks later-stage hook/surface packaging for matured lines
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:231:- our space tolerates latent meaning longer than Claude Code surface packaging
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:267:- Claude Code: delayed plugin/hook/agent surface
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:278:Ralph, Claude Code, and autoresearch all know how to make a line show itself quickly, but they each do it by sacrificing a different kind of openness. Ralph sacrifices ambiguity by cutting the task down until it can be closed. Claude Code sacrifices latency by surfacing patterns early as commands, hooks, and packaged behavior. autoresearch sacrifices ambiguity even harder by locking the experiment frame and asking one narrow mutable surface to prove itself against a hard metric.
docs/reports/three_reference_folders_line_formation_reread_v0.md:282:So the important insight is not that we need to become Ralph, Claude Code, or autoresearch. The insight is that once our own lines have thickened enough, we can finally see what those references really are: not competing cores, but attachable parts for later. Ralph can become an execution memory rail. Claude Code can become a pluginized intervention surface. autoresearch can become a bounded experiment harness. They are useful precisely because they are not our foundation.
